# `nudge` moves a sound parameter by exact steps and brings it back: NOT on the TRIG page, two
# steps up and down, then five up and back in two turns. Each screen is taken 3.5 s after the last
# turn, when stock's value overlay (title = the parameter's name) is gone. Ends as it began, but
# a turned parameter marks the kit as changed, so: state changes.
name: link-nudge-and-back
state: changes

# TRIG pressed on its own page shows its second page, and the unit keeps that choice: come from another.
key AMP
key TRIG
wait 3500                       # the page's name leaves the title bar
screen rest
nudge A +2
wait 750                        # stock draws a turn up to half a second late
screen turned                   # value overlay up
expect turned != rest
wait 3500
screen up
expect up != rest
nudge A -2
wait 3500
screen down
expect down == rest
nudge A +5
nudge A -3
nudge A -2
wait 3500
screen again
expect again == rest
